  "presentation_summary": [
    "27-year-old woman with AML underwent haplo-identical allogeneic HSCT and remained deeply immunosuppressed with very low CD4 count and ongoing mycophenolate exposure.",
    "Three weeks after donor lymphocyte infusion and around five months after transplant, she was admitted with fever 38.5 C, nausea, vomiting, weight loss, anorexia, and severe oral candidiasis.",
    "Initial labs showed anemia, leukopenia, thrombocytopenia, CRP 86 mg/L, hypokalemia, creatinine 1.06 mg/dL, normal bilirubin, AST 228 U/L, and ALT 136 U/L.",
    "During hospitalization she developed diarrhea, rash, hepatomegaly with pain, ascites, edema, fever to 40 C, severe hepatic cytolysis/cholestasis, pancytopenia, and DIC after liver biopsy.",
    "She died from hepatic failure; postmortem virology and liver pathology confirmed adenovirus infection by PCR and immunohistochemistry."
  ],
